      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "If $U=\\{2,4,6,8,…,20\\}$ is the universal set and $B=\\{4,8,12,16,20\\},$ then the complement of $B$ is",
      "original_html_sha256": "cd7fe696269100f960bdede786c9f553754b2804fc67fa04df012d442c936c40",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/cd7fe696269100f960bdede786c9f553754b2804fc67fa04df012d442c936c40.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $2,$ $6,$ $10,$ $14,$ and $18.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}=\\{2,6,10,14,18\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "42a39b8dedd8f9264e72391a248f6b7f2969fee5068e710fbdcfabb0f50ab40b",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
